{#
  This file IS the policy: /etc/logrotate.d/rsyslog is the packaged rsyslog Conffile and the file
  logrotate already reads for /var/log/syslog, mail.log, kern.log, auth.log, user.log and cron.log.
  A second, role-named stanza cannot be added beside it — logrotate 3.22 refuses a path two stanzas
  name (`error: zz-candidate:1 duplicate log entry for /var/log/syslog`, `found error in file
  zz-candidate, skipping`, exit 1, logrotate.service failed), so owning these paths means rendering
  the file that owns them and changing nothing but the retention knobs.

  dpkg behaviour this relies on: this path is a listed Conffile (`dpkg-query -W -f='${Conffiles}'
  rsyslog` names it and the md5 of the packaged bytes), and a locally-modified Conffile is KEPT on
  package upgrade — dpkg does not silently restore it. The read-leg in tasks/pi.yml is the canary for
  the day that stops holding: it asserts the retention logrotate REPORTS, not that this file exists.

  Retention, ruled by the owner for this host: size-triggered with one retained generation, sized against the
  mount. `/var/log` is a tmpfs (see pi_var_log_opts), so rotation moves bytes within the same
  filesystem and a calendar retention has no bound. `daily` gives one rotation per period, `maxsize`
  is the trip-wire for a chatty day, `rotate 1` keeps the retained generation to one. Worst case is
  therefore ~2x maxsize for this stanza; the other five paths are two orders of magnitude quieter
  (measured on the Pi: syslog 5.1 M against auth.log 0.69 M, user.log 0.09 M, kern.log 5 K, cron.log
  16 K over the same period), so the mount keeps real headroom. If a non-syslog path ever becomes the
  fat one, split this stanza instead of raising maxsize.

  Everything else — compress/delaycompress/missingok/notifempty/sharedscripts/postrotate — is the
  packaged stanza verbatim, postrotate included: it is what tells rsyslog to reopen its files.
#}
# Managed by Ansible — roles/home_assistant. Retention is sized against the /var/log tmpfs.
/var/log/syslog
/var/log/mail.log
/var/log/kern.log
/var/log/auth.log
/var/log/user.log
/var/log/cron.log
{
	rotate 1
	daily
	maxsize {{ pi_var_log_maxsize }}
	missingok
	notifempty
	compress
	delaycompress
	sharedscripts
	postrotate
		/usr/lib/rsyslog/rsyslog-rotate
	endscript
}
